[43.302427, "o", "[approval] bash: ls /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/ 2>&1 | head -20 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash ls /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/ 2>&1 | head -20\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 8 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: ls /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip/ 2>&1 | head -5 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash ls /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip/ 2>&1 | head -5\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 9 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: python3 -c \"import pip._internal.cli.main\" 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash python3 -c \"import pip._internal.cli.main\" 2>&1\r\n    ✗ bash — exit 1\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 10 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ Found the problem. The `pip3` binary exists and points to the right Pytho…\r\n  │ Let me restore it:\r\n[approval] bash: python3 -m ensurepip --default-pip 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash python3 -m ensurepip --default-pip 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 11 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ That didn't re-install it since it thinks it's a"]
[43.302524, "o", "lready there. Let me forc…\r\n[approval] bash: rm -rf /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info && python3 -m ensurepip --default-pip 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash rm -rf /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info &&…\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 12 tool call(s) so far\r\n  [tools] 12 call(s) without changing a file — nudging to decide\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 12 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: pip3 --version 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash pip3 --version 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 13 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: pip3 install --dry-run requests 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash pip3 install --dry-run requests 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 14 tool call(s) so far\r\nFixed. Here's what was wrong and what I did:\r\n\r\n**Problem:** The `pip` package files had been deleted from `/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/`, but the `.dist-info` metadata directory (`pip-24.3.1.dist-info`) was still there. This left a dangling `"]
[43.302557, "o", "pip3` binary that pointed to a missing `pip` module — `pip` thought it was installed (because of the metadata) but the actual code was gone.\r\n\r\n**Fix:** I removed the orphaned `pip-24.3.1.dist-info` directory and re-ran `python3 -m ensurepip --default-pip`, which restored the full pip package. pip is now working again (`pip3 --version` confirms 24.3.1).\r\n\r\n[result] role=implementor model=qwen3.6-35b tools=14 surface=767eb34430d9\r\n"]
